ing up, down, left or right through non-wall cells. Rooms that cannot reach any gate stay <code>INF</code>. The function returns nothing; the judge inspects <code>rooms</code> afterwards.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p><pre>Input: rooms = [[INF,-1,0,INF],[INF,INF,INF,-1],[INF,-1,INF,-1],[0,-1,INF,INF]]\nOutput: [[3,-1,0,1],[2,2,1,-1],[1,-1,2,-1],[0,-1,3,4]]</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p><pre>Input: rooms = [[-1]]\nOutput: [[-1]]</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p><pre>Input: rooms = [[0,INF,INF]]\nOutput: [[0,1,2]]</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p><ul><li><code>m == rooms.length</code></li><li><code>n == rooms[i].length</code></li><li><code>1 &lt;= m, n &lt;= 250</code></li><li><code>rooms[i][j] is -1, 0 or 2147483647</code></li></ul>","exampleTestcases":"[[2147483647,-1,0,2147483647],[2147483647,2147483647,2147483647,-1],[2147483647,-1,2147483647,-1],[0,-1,2147483647,2147483647]]\n[[-1]]\n[[0,2147483647,2147483647]]","metaData":"{\"name\": \"wallsAndGates\", \"params\": [{\"name\": \"rooms\", \"type\": \"integer[][]\"}], \"return\": {\"type\": \"void\"}}","codeSnippets":[{"langSlug":"python3","code":"class Solution:\n    def wallsAndGates(self, rooms: List[List[int]]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Do not return anything, modify rooms in-place instead.\n        \"\"\"\n        \n"}]}}